# AIOS — Repository policy for generated non-source artifacts
#
# Scope: generated non-source artifacts. Generated bytecode and its cache
# directories are reproducible outputs of running the source, not source.
# They are excluded so that commit boundaries stay deterministic and every
# tracked file is an authored artifact.
#
# Authority: repository structure is outside the authority of both the
# Engineering Constitution (§0 — it "does not specify ... repository
# structure") and the Canonical Domain Model (§8 — it does not "define,
# imply, or constrain repository layout"). This file is a repository
# convention only. It introduces no entity, no relationship, no invariant,
# and no governance authority, and it constrains no architecture.
#
# This policy is deliberately narrow. It governs only the artifacts named
# below. Any broader exclusion requires its own authorization.

__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo

# Legacy execution traces — generated runtime output of the pre-freeze
# execution harness, not authored source. Disposition EXCLUDE, per the
# Repository Curation Review.
execution/traces/
